  "result": "The issue is open: https://github.com/acme/textstats/issues/13\n\n- **Title:** \"word_count returns 1 for empty string (should be 0)\"\n- **Where:** `word_count` is in `textstats/__init__.py`, lines 4-6.\n- **Cause:** it uses `len(text.split(\" \"))`, and `\"\".split(\" \")` returns `['']`, which has length 1. The same split also miscounts repeated spaces (`\"a  b\"` gives 3). `average_word_length` in the same file already uses `text.split()`.\n- **Acceptance criteria:** `word_count(\"\") == 0`, the existing test still passes, and a regression test is added.\n\nI didn't change any code.\n\nThe repo's `origin` remote is a local path (`/tmp/model-router-bench-kb6qfrqj/origin.git`), but the issue went to `acme/textstats` on GitHub. The subagent didn't say why it chose that repo, so please check it's the tracker you meant.",
